At Tue, 21 Oct 2003 13:32:10 +0200 (CEST),
Jaroslav wrote:
> 
> > very short while a write will block for more than one second. Are those
> > ALSA related problems, or hardware ones ?
> 
> You said that you're using an USB device. It might be a problem with our
> USB driver. Also, USB devices are working with 1ms periods at the physical
> level, so transferring 32 frames does not make probably sense anyway.

this should be ok, since the sample rate is 8k Hz (although
RT-scheduling would be needed for 4ms periods.)

but 1ms period alignment is important:  if you want a RT process with
the USB audio device, choose the sample rate with multiple of 1000.
for example, avoid 44.1kHz, but use 48k instead.


